{"id":86817,"title":"PDF Geometry and Attribute Compression for Voxel Scenes","url":"https://timothykol.com/pub/compression.pdf","final_url":"https://timothykol.com/pub/compression.pdf","year":null,"kind":"web","source":"ddg","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"8aa6b183601b48f56287c7dc8b7bfafe914b7bd4e232fce51b7ee2230dc25fb8","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"url","fetched_at":1793148612.9972603,"text_chars":54070,"abstract":"timothykol.com\n\nhttps://timothykol.com › pub › compression.pdf\n\nPDF Geometry and Attribute Compression for Voxel Scenes\nBy decoupling geometry and voxel data via a novel mapping scheme, we are able to apply the DAG principle to encode the topology, while using a palette-based compression for the voxel attributes, leading to a drastic memory reduction. Our method outperforms existing state-of-the-art techniques and is well-suited for GPU architectures.","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["https://timothykol.com/pub/compression.pdf","http://web.archive.org/web/20240726112117/https://graphics.tudelft.nl/Publications-new/2016/DKBTE16/voxel_compression.pdf","https://graphics.tudelft.nl/Publications-new/2016/DKBTE16/voxel_compression.pdf"],"cited_by":[{"path":"1873-palette-compression.md","name":"Palette Compression","k":1},{"path":"1893-decoupled-dag-with-palette-compression.md","name":"Decoupled DAG with Palette Compression","k":1},{"path":"1872-decoupled-svo-compression.md","name":"Decoupled SVO Compression","k":1},{"path":"1761-voxel-attribute-decoupling.md","name":"Voxel Attribute Decoupling","k":1},{"path":"1819-offset-compression.md","name":"Offset Compression","k":1},{"path":"1770-pointer-compression.md","name":"Pointer Compression","k":1},{"path":"1912-attribute-quantization.md","name":"Attribute Quantization","k":1}]}